  "id": "self-categorization-theory",
  "term": "self-categorization theory",
  "definition": "Self-categorization theory is a social psychology theory proposing that how people define themselves in relation to a group influences their experience and behavior in group settings. In the packet, it is used to explain why people who identify more strongly with a crowd may feel less crowded and report more positive emotion.",
