      "reasons": [
        "The first sentence makes a broad, general claim that the theory “propos[es]” how people define themselves in relation to a group influences “their experience and behavior in group settings.” The packet only describes self-categorization theory being used to predict emotional responses to crowding as a function of social identification; it does not support the specific “behavior in group settings” component or the general self-definition/behavior framing. ",
